    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## The Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file because the `--ci` flag was being consumed by the main `frai` program's option parser and never passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n## The Solution\nI modified the `gate` command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to use `process.argv` directly instead of relying on Commander.js's parsed `args` parameter. This ensures all arguments\u2014including flags like `--ci`\u2014are correctly forwarded to the delegated `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**Key change:** Instead of using the `args` parameter that Commander parsed, the handler now extracts the raw arguments from `process.argv` after the 'gate' keyword, preserving all flags and options.\n\n## Verification\nBoth commands now work correctly:\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` \u2192 creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 `frai-gate init --ci` \u2192 still works as before\n\nThe fix is minimal and focused on the delegation mechanism, without changing the `frai-gate` package as instructed.",
